---
import Stop from "../Stop.astro";
import Shot from "../Shot.astro";
---

<Stop
  id="publish"
  title="You choose what reaches the merge request"
  log="4 findings → GitLab"
  crosses
  status={{ label: "Published", variant: "success" }}
>
  <div class="publish">
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Nothing is posted on its own. You publish the findings worth a reviewer's time, one at
        a time or all at once, and each becomes an inline discussion on its file and line in
        the MR. A finding already published is never posted twice, so you can come back later
        and publish more.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you want the comments to sound like you, save samples of your writing as a voice
        profile. 4R rewrites the summary and each finding in that voice, and you publish the
        rewritten card or the original, card by card.
      </p>
    </div>
    <Shot
      name="publish"
      full
      width={1024}
      height={576}
      alt="Two findings for MR !142: a medium Risk finding already marked Published, and the high, blocking Resilience finding still showing its Publish button, with a version rewritten in the author's voice selected."
      caption="Each finding is published on its own, or all at once."
    />
  </div>
</Stop>

<style>
  .publish {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2rem;
  }
  @media (min-width: 60rem) {
    .publish {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(16rem, 0.8fr) minmax(0, 1.6fr);
      gap: 2.5rem;
      align-items: start;
    }
  }
</style>
